  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n- Cold mornings with valley fog for much of the rest of the week. \n\n- A warming trend for high temperatures through the end of the \n  week with Friday 10 to 15 degrees above average. \n\n- Cold front coming this weekend brings gusty winds to northwest\n  MT on Saturday. \n\nHigh pressure slowly builds over the Northern Rockies, while low\npressure develops over Southern California. This is a blocking\npattern and will slow the progression of weather systems from \nwest to east. Expect continued cool to cold mornings with patchy \nfog, especially along river valleys. Afternoon high temperatures \nslowly warm to the low 70s by Friday in western MT, or what is \nthe average high for the 3rd week of September. Enjoy a small \nreturn to late summer. \n\nSaturday a mostly dry, cold front breaks down the ridge and\n'blocking pattern'. Expect a very breezy afternoon, especially\nnorth of I-90. Winds in the high terrain could gust 40 to 50 mph,\nwhile valleys experience gusts 20 to 30 mph. Humidities remain in\nthe 30s, please exercise caution with any fall burning. \n\nThe pattern is expected to remain progressive to start next week,\nwith greatly varying model outcomes. There remains many questions\nabout how far south the next trough digs, how cold the associated air\nmass will be, and how much moisture is available for\nprecipitation. More to come.",
